As far as the textronix workstation is concerned, I don't think it's
a matter of needing to re-compile the program. It seems more of an issue
of not having chosen the correct terminal type.

If this thing is a derivative of AT&T unix, there should be some way of setting
the terminal type. If he/she uses an xterm window, then the proper term-type
could be vt100. (Most unix you can type "set term=vt100" at the prompt. then
start hack.)   If this doesn't work, let me know...

